,"index.title":"Timeline index","tasks.title":"Background tasks","tasks.generation":"Generation \xB7 {step}","tasks.none":"No task running.","tour.title":"Getting started","tour.subtitle":"The main path through Video Producer","tour.project.title":"Create a project","tour.project.text":"File \u203A New project, or start from this starter project.","tour.direction.title":"Set the global direction","tour.direction.text":"Director IA \u203A Direction: world, characters, photography, palette, pacing.","tour.references.title":"Add the references","tour.references.text":"Director IA \u203A References: identities, 3D sets, motion guides.","tour.shots.title":"Split the film into shots","tour.shots.text":"Storyboard: write the synopsis, propose a breakdown, adjust the shot prompts.","tour.drafts.title":"Generate drafts","tour.drafts.text":"Production bar: Draft quality, then \u201CGenerate selection\u201D. The estimate shows GPU time and quota.","tour.final.title":"Pick and make final","tour.final.text":"Inspector \u203A Takes: compare, pick, then \u201CMake final\u201D on the best take.","tour.mix.title":"Edit, match and mix","tour.mix.text":"Fades on clips, color matching in the inspector, console in Mix.","tour.delivery.title":"Prepare delivery","tour.delivery.text":"File \u203A Export: video, FCPXML / OTIO / EDL, subtitles.","simulations.title":"Simulated features","simulations.subtitle":"What really works and what is simulated","simulations.intro":"Editing, selection, the inspector, fades, the prompt library, the assistant, conflict checks, AI generation and takes, exports, the 3D scene (scenes built from an image, imported splats and Blender files, the camera, captures and reference videos) and the console work for real. The following are simulated and carry the {badge} badge:","simulations.identity.title":"Identity score","simulations.identity.text":"The identity similarity between two shots, in the continuity check and in the assistant\u2019s review, is simulated. The color match really analyzes the images.","simulations.lipSync.title":"Lip sync","simulations.lipSync.text":"No lip sync is computed: the lip sync options of the Sound design workshop stay in the project and change neither the takes nor the export.","simulations.voice.title":"Generated voices and dialogue","simulations.voice.text":"The Sound design workshop generates no voice, dialogue or sound: preparing is simulated and what you hear is a simple synthesis in the browser. The dialogue text feeds the subtitles, and imported audio files play for real.","simulations.console.title":"Console automation and processing","simulations.console.text":"The Auto button only switches a mode: no automation curve is recorded. Pan, inserts, sends and the master bus are heard in the browser but are not applied to the exported video, which keeps the gain, the track faders, mute, solo and the fades.","simulations.formats.title":"ProRes, H.265 and stems","simulations.formats.text":"The master file (ProRes), the archive (H.265) and the audio stems are simulated: no file is written. The web and social MP4 videos and the FCPXML, OTIO, EDL and SRT files are real.","simulations.guidance.title":"Guidance of the Control videos","simulations.guidance.text":"The guidance strength of a Control video stays in the project but does not change the takes: the engine reads the guide video as it is.","open.title":"Open a project","open.current":"Current","recap.title":"Generation summary","recap.global":"Global direction","recap.allVideos":"all videos","recap.local":"Shot prompts","recap.quote":"\u201C{text}\u201D","recap.none":"None.","recap.refs":"References and Control videos","recap.scopeGlobal":"global","recap.scopeLocal":"local","recap.frame":"Frame {role} at {time} \xB7 {strength} %","recap.control":"Control video \u201C{name}\u201D \xB7 guidance {guidance} %","properties.title":"Project properties","properties.name":"Name","properties.aspect":"Aspect ratio","properties.resolution":"Resolution"